---
description: Authentication and authorization rules
globs: apps/api/src/auth/**/*.ts, apps/api/src/common/guards/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Tokens
- Access: JWT (RS256 or EdDSA), 10 min TTL, claims: `sub`, `sid`, `roles`, `kid`.
- Refresh: opaque 256-bit random, stored as Argon2id hash in `refresh_tokens(userId, jti, hash, expiresAt, replacedBy)`.
- Rotation: every `/refresh` issues new pair and sets `replacedBy`. Reuse of a retired token revokes the family.

# Registration/login
- Argon2id for password hashing.
- Verify email via signed time-limited token (jose).
- TOTP 2FA with recovery codes (hashed).
- Login rate limit: 5/min/IP + 10/hour/account (Redis).

# Authorization
- RBAC roles: `user`, `pro`, `admin`. Attribute checks: resource owner or admin.
- Guards: `JwtAuthGuard`, `RolesGuard`, `OwnershipGuard`. Compose via `@UseGuards(...)`.
- Never trust `userId` from the request body; read from `req.user`.

# API keys
- Separate table, prefix-displayed key (`ak_live_...`), stored as Argon2id hash.
- Scope per key (`read:market`, `trade:paper`, `admin`). Deny by default.
